put('0930','p1',S('main','exact','Cov(X,Y)=E[XY]-E[X]E[Y]. Substituting Y=X² gives E[X³]-E[X]E[X²]=0-0 E[X²].','Cov(X,Y)=0.','Scalar covariance; finite third moment in the usual expectation sense implies finite second moment. The asserted dependence need not hold for degenerate X or constant X², but that does not alter covariance.'))
put('0930','p2',S('main','symbolic','Let z=ax+by. E[z]=aμx+bμy. Center z: a(x-μx)+b(y-μy). Its outer product has a²Σx+b²Σy and two ab cross terms; independence makes both cross terms zero. Gaussianity is supplied.','z~N(aμx+bμy, a²Σx+b²Σy).','x,y must have the same dimension d; means d×1 and covariance d×d. If covariance is positive definite, density is (2π)^(-d/2)|Σz|^(-1/2) exp[-(z-μz)ᵀΣz⁻¹(z-μz)/2]; otherwise use a degenerate Gaussian measure.'))
put('0930','p3',S('main','symbolic','Write H=(y1,…,yt). In full generality let mw=E[w|H], QH=Cov(w|H), K=Cov(xt,w|H). Conditional linearity gives E[xt+1|H]=Aμt+mw and Cov(xt+1|H)=AΣtAᵀ+QH+AK+KᵀAᵀ. For fresh process noise independent of (xt,H), mw=0,QH=Q,K=0.','Under fresh-noise independence: N(Aμt,AΣtAᵀ+Q).','A maps state to next-state dimension; the displayed covariance is square in next-state dimension and symmetric. Gaussianity is given.',unresolved=['Independence of w from the state alone does not logically establish independence after conditioning on H; a fresh-noise or equivalent conditional independence condition is needed to uniquely deduce the usual formula.'],assumptions=['The usual prediction formula assumes w independent of (xt,H).']))
put('0930','p4',S('main','proof','E[(x-μ)²]=E[x²-2μx+μ²]=E[x²]-2μE[x]+μ²E[1]=E[x²]-2μ²+μ².','Var(x)=E[x²]-(E[x])².','Requires a finite second moment for an ordinary finite variance; constants leave expectation unchanged.'))
put('0930','p5',S('main','symbolic','Condition on x. Then Ax+b is constant and w retains N(0,Q) because w is independent of x. Translation changes only the mean.','p(y|x)=N(y|Ax+b,Q).','A:E×D, x:D×1, b:E×1, Q:E×E. For Q≻0 use (2π)^(-E/2)|Q|^(-1/2) exp[-(y-Ax-b)ᵀQ⁻¹(y-Ax-b)/2]; the prior covariance of x does not enter this conditional.'))
put('0930','p6',S('main','symbolic','E[y]=A E[x]+b+E[w]=Aμx+b. Then y-E[y]=A(x-μx)+w. Expanding its outer product gives AΣxAᵀ+AE[(x-μx)wᵀ]+E[w(x-μx)ᵀ]Aᵀ+E[wwᵀ]. Independence and centering remove the middle terms.','μy=Aμx+b; Σy=AΣxAᵀ+Q; y~N(μy,Σy).','A:E×D, Σx:D×D, Σy,Q:E×E; b affects only the mean. Covariance is positive semidefinite since uᵀΣyu=(Aᵀu)ᵀΣx(Aᵀu)+uᵀQu≥0.'))
put('0930','p7',S('a','symbolic','Fix y; Cy is constant and v is independent of y.','p(z|y)=N(z|Cy,R).','If C:F×E then z:F×1 and R:F×F; ordinary density requires R≻0.'),S('b','symbolic','E[z]=CE[y]=C(Aμx+b). Centering gives z-μz=C(y-μy)+v; covariance expands to CΣyCᵀ+R because independence kills cross terms.','μz=C(Aμx+b); Σz=C(AΣxAᵀ+Q)Cᵀ+R; z~N(μz,Σz).','CΣyCᵀ and R are both F×F. Given Gaussianity; zero noise recovers covariance of deterministic linear transformation.'))
put('0930','p8',S('main','proof','For N≥1, Σij(xi-xj)²=Σij xi²+Σij xj²-2Σij xixj=2NΣi xi²-2(Σi xi)². Divide by N² and factor 2.','N⁻²Σij(xi-xj)²=2[N⁻¹Σi xi²-(N⁻¹Σi xi)²].','The double sum is over ordered pairs including i=j, which contribute zero. For N=1 both sides vanish.'))
put('1007','p1',S('a','qualitative','Draw one 6-vector θi~N(0,I6/4). Hold that single vector fixed and evaluate fi(xj)=φ(xj)ᵀθi at all 200 input locations.','A parameter draw followed by evaluation across the grid produces one function sample.','The same θi must be used at every xj; independent draws at each x would not produce one polynomial.'),S('b','exact','The monomials x⁰ through x⁵ require six coefficients.','θ∈R⁶.','φ(x) is 6×1, hence θᵀφ(x) is scalar.'),S('c','symbolic','At fixed x, f=φ(x)ᵀθ has mean 0 and variance φᵀ(I6/4)φ=(1/4)Σk=0⁵ x^(2k). The shading comes from this prior parameter uncertainty propagated through the polynomial.','Pointwise prior credible intervals for noiseless function values, with supplied inner 67% and outer 95% levels.','No observation noise is included. Different x values are correlated through Cov(f(x),f(x′))=(1/4)Σk=0⁵(xx′)^k. Exact central Gaussian half-width for mass p is Φ⁻¹((1+p)/2) times the standard deviation; 67% is not exactly ±1σ.'))
